# ---- Capacitor native shell (EPIC-6) ----
# android/ IS committed: the native project is source, not build output, and regenerating
# it with `cap add android` would discard any hand-edited Gradle or manifest change.
#
# Nothing under android/ is listed here on purpose. Capacitor ships its own
# android/.gitignore which already covers .gradle/, build/, local.properties, captures/,
# the copied web assets and the synced config. Duplicating those rules here would mean two
# places to keep in step, and the copy at this level would win silently when they drift.
#
# Only the pieces Capacitor does not know about are listed:

# icon and splash SOURCES, regenerated by scripts/make-app-assets.mjs. The generated
# res/ images under android/ are committed; these 2732px originals are not.
/assets/

# Play Store listing graphics, regenerated by scripts/make-play-assets.mjs. Deterministic
# from the script and the design tokens, so the script is the thing worth versioning.
/play/

# Signing material must never be committed, whatever directory it lands in.
#
# Losing the upload key is unrecoverable without Play App Signing, and committing it is
# worse than losing it: anyone with the repo could then ship an update that Play and every
# installed device would accept as genuine. Both of these are anchored so a nested path
# cannot slip through, and keystore.properties holds the passwords that open the key.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
keystore.properties
android/keystore.properties
